WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:04.292
Have you recovered
after that explosive ending

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:06.500
to Money Heist Part 5,
Volume 1?

00:00:06.583 --> 00:00:08.208
Us neither,
if we're being honest.

00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:09.917
And we totally understand

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.417
if you've got lots
of questions,

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.750
probably starting with why?

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:17.042
And then moving swiftly onto

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:20.875
when is Money Heist Part 5,
Volume 2 coming out please?

00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:22.333
I can't wait any longer.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:24.875
We'll forgive you
for missing the bit

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.333
where
this information appears

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.042
in big red letters
right at the end.

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:28.958
You were probably

00:00:29.042 --> 00:00:30.792
breathing heavily
into a paper bag

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:31.708
and that's okay.

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:34.500
Money Heist Part 5,
Volume 2 arrives on Netflix

00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:35.667
on the 3 December.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.542
Five final episodes
that will bring this story

00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:39.792
to its conclusion.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.458
Is Lisbon an undercover cop?

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.750
This is a big question.

00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:47.792
We know from Part 1
of Money Heist

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.833
what a skilled negotiator
Raquel Murillo is.

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.750
She even outwits Tamayo

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.000
and saves the robbers
in Part 5,

00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.708
while the Professor's
out of action.

00:00:55.792 --> 00:00:58.917
We also know she's a woman
of principle and loyalty.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.042
Yes, the Professor's clever,
handsome, and charismatic,

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:02.958
offering Raquel

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:05.083
a romantic dream
of wealth and freedom,

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.000
but would she really
throw her entire career away

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:09.333
just for one man?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.750
Or is Raquel's
indoctrination

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:12.792
into the gang,

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:14.500
her adoption
of the codename Lisbon,

00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:15.625
and her acceptance

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.167
into the Professor's
trusted inner circle

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.667
all part of a wider plan?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.292
If she is
still working undercover

00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:25.625
for the Spanish authorities,
Raquel has hit the jackpot.

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:27.833
The Professor has let her
in on all his plans

00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:29.458
and she'll have
enough evidence

00:01:29.542 --> 00:01:30.750
to take him down.

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:33.500
But the truth is
we just don't know.

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:35.500
If Lisbon is a police mole,

00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:37.375
then we can add
Oscar-winning actress

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:39.167
to her sizable
list of skills

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.500
as her emotional attachment,

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:42.042
not just to the Professor,

00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:44.750
but the entire gang,
is plain to see.

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.167
My presence
changes everything.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.958
Extraction
is the priority now.

00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:50.542
Does the Professor
truly love Lisbon?

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.083
On the other side
of the equation

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.208
we have the Professor,

00:01:53.292 --> 00:01:54.917
a master of foresight
and planning

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.333
and tactical genius
and inspiring orator.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.125
But a man who quite clearly
has a strong emotional bond

00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:02.375
with those
he now considers his family.

00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:04.292
Look at how much
they all mean to him.

00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:06.167
You can see it
in his face...

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.500
hear it in his voice...

00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.500
I'm sorry, Raquel.

00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:11.583
I'm so sorry, Rio.

00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:15.750
I'm sorry, Palermo.

00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:19.333
Okay, we get it.
Thanks, Professor.

00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:22.458
At this stage,
the fact he loves Lisbon

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.875
is not really up for debate

00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:26.500
as evidenced by his reaction
when he thought she'd died

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:27.958
at the end of series 3.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.042
But whether or not
the romantic relationship

00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:33.375
has taken root in
a game of cat and mouse,

00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:34.500
the one they started

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.083
during the royal mint heist
in series 1,

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:38.667
is a question the answer

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.333
to which we won't know
with 100% certainty

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:45.083
until Part 5, Volume 2
arrives on the 3 December.

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.708
Will Alicia join the gang?

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:50.958
Alicia Sierra,
disgraced police inspector,

00:02:51.042 --> 00:02:54.083
torturer, lone wolf, mother,

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.042
but will she ever be
part of the gang?

00:02:56.125 --> 00:02:58.292
It's difficult to see
any other route for Sierra

00:02:58.375 --> 00:02:59.500
at this point.

00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:02.125
Publicly shamed
and betrayed by Tamayo

00:03:02.208 --> 00:03:03.958
and her former
police colleagues,

00:03:04.042 --> 00:03:05.333
she's essentially on the run

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:07.292
with her new born child,
Victoria.

00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:09.292
A logical move would be

00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:11.125
to join forces
with the Professor.

00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:12.750
He's the one
with the dirt on Tamayo

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.042
that could clear her name,

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:16.292
plus her attempts
to comfort the Professor

00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:17.833
after the events
at the bank,

00:03:17.917 --> 00:03:20.000
would suggest
her icy hatred for him

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:21.542
is thawing somewhat.

00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:25.375
But Alicia Sierra is nothing
if not unpredictable.

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:31.667
She's also smart,
resourceful,

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.500
and already has displayed
a willingness

00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:35.833
to do whatever it takes
to get the job done.

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:37.375
Checkmate, son of a bitch.

00:03:39.625 --> 00:03:41.750
Is Arturo Roman still alive?

00:03:42.333 --> 00:03:44.208
It doesn't look great
for Arturo, does it?

00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:45.750
Gunned down by Stockholm

00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:48.083
after a bungled attempt
at playing the hero,

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:49.958
the last time
we saw Arturo Roman

00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:52.000
he was being wheeled
into an ambulance

00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:53.875
with a bullet
still lodged in his chest.

00:03:54.708 --> 00:03:56.833
As Palermo
succinctly puts it,

00:03:56.917 --> 00:03:58.292
his chances aren't great.

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:00.458
He was dead a minute ago
and he'll be dead again

00:04:00.542 --> 00:04:03.208
when you stop blowing air
into his lungs.

00:04:03.292 --> 00:04:06.250
Still, this is Arturo Roman
we're talking about.

00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:07.792
An abusive scumbag

00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:09.500
with a special talent
for showing up

00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:11.875
at the most
inconvenient moments.

00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:14.292
We wouldn't be surprised
if he had some part to play.

00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:15.458
Even if it's just

00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:17.458
as the trauma-induced
hallucinations

00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:19.000
of a guilt-ridden Monica.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.000
What happened to Tatiana?

00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:28.375
The character of Tatiana

00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.125
has been the subject
of much speculation.

00:04:31.208 --> 00:04:33.500
There are some who think she
and Alicia Sierra

00:04:33.583 --> 00:04:35.167
are one in the same person.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.833
A fan theory dismissed
by actress Najwa Nimri,

00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:39.542
but it's certainly possible

00:04:39.625 --> 00:04:42.208
Tatiana could have
a significant role to play

00:04:42.292 --> 00:04:43.125
before the end.

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:44.167
The widow of Berlin

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.042
and therefore
the ex brother-in-law

00:04:46.125 --> 00:04:48.500
of the Professor,
Tatiana is important

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:50.750
in that she almost certainly
has knowledge

00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.167
of the bank heist plan,

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.375
seeing as it was Berlin's
brain child to begin with.

00:04:55.458 --> 00:04:57.583
How this will play out
is anyone's guess.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.500
But eagle-eye viewers
will have noticed

00:04:59.583 --> 00:05:01.417
the look she shared
with Rafael

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.125
as they sealed the way
with stolen Viking gold.

00:05:04.208 --> 00:05:06.542
If you really want
something in life,

00:05:08.292 --> 00:05:10.167
you have to steal it
from whomever has it.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.500
What will the Professor's
next move be?

00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:16.375
This is the big question.

00:05:16.875 --> 00:05:19.417
Tragedy has truck
and the gang is desolated,

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.792
but for all the heart break,

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:22.708
the robbers are in
a far better position

00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:25.500
than when we joined them
at the beginning of Part 5.

00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:27.042
The Professor
is back in the game

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:30.208
and holds important leverage
over Coronel Tamayo.

00:05:30.292 --> 00:05:31.417
Sagasta, Gandía,

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.208
and their team
of special operatives,

00:05:33.292 --> 00:05:34.167
are defeated.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.250
Alicia Sierra knows
the extraction plan

00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:37.875
for the gold, but crucially,

00:05:37.958 --> 00:05:39.958
the Spanish authorities
do not.

00:05:40.042 --> 00:05:41.292
And last we saw,

00:05:41.375 --> 00:05:43.542
the melting operation
was back on.

00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:46.083
Either way,
the Professor's priority

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.000
will surely be
to extract the gang

00:05:48.083 --> 00:05:49.375
with no more casualties.

00:05:49.875 --> 00:05:51.625
Well, if that's with
or without the gold,

00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:52.667
only time will tell.

00:05:57.042 --> 00:05:58.583
What's the meaning
of "Bella Ciao"?

00:05:58.667 --> 00:06:01.208
and why do the robbers
always sing it?

00:06:01.792 --> 00:06:04.083
The unofficial anthem
of Money Heist and the tune

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:06.167
we've unashamedly belted out
in the shower

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.417
pretty much every day
since Money Heist debuted

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.708
in 2017,

00:06:09.792 --> 00:06:12.750
"Bella Ciao" a traditional
Italian folk song

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:15.542
that translates
as, "goodbye, beautiful".

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.542
Allegedly
first sung by women

00:06:17.625 --> 00:06:19.375
working in the fields
of Northern Italy

00:06:19.458 --> 00:06:20.667
in order to pass time,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.125
"Bella Ciao" took on
political significance

00:06:23.208 --> 00:06:26.583
after being adopted
as an antifascist anthem.

00:06:26.667 --> 00:06:27.875
The song became synonymous

00:06:27.958 --> 00:06:29.667
with the Italian
Partisan Resistance

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.667
who fought against the Nazis
and the Italian fascists

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:34.000
during WWII.

00:06:34.542 --> 00:06:36.875
Since then, "Bella Ciao"
has been sung worldwide

00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:38.208
as a hymn of freedom,

00:06:38.292 --> 00:06:40.083
an anthem
representing rebellion

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:41.208
and liberation.

00:06:41.292 --> 00:06:43.167
So, it makes total sense
why Money Heist's

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.667
beloved family
of bank robbers

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.083
would adopt "Bella Ciao"
as their own.

00:06:47.167 --> 00:06:50.375
Here's a group of outcasts
ostracised by society,

00:06:50.458 --> 00:06:51.667
fighting for their freedom

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.042
against
the perceived tyranny

00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:55.083
of the oppressive
Spanish state.

00:06:55.167 --> 00:06:56.208
Take it away, gang.

